# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/).

## [Unreleased]

## [v1.7.2-dtc] - 2026-09-10

### Added
- DTC (Device Tree Compiler) 1.7.2 cross-compilation support
  - GitHub Actions workflow for automated builds (4 architectures × 2 link types)
  - Build script `scripts/build-dtc-musl.sh` with architecture validation
  - Package script `scripts/package-dtc-musl.sh` with complete toolset
  - Includes dtc, fdtdump, fdtget, fdtput, fdtoverlay, and libfdt library
  - Minimal dependencies build with NO_PYTHON=1 and NO_YAML=1
  - Comprehensive documentation in `docs/dtc-setup.md`
  - Support for static (no dependencies) and dynamic (musl-linked) variants
  - Functional testing in CI for x86_64 target (both static and dynamic)
  - Release tag format: `v1.7.2-dtc`
  - Two-stage build process for static linking to avoid shared library generation
  - Manual install for static builds to prevent libfdt target from regenerating .so files

### Changed
- Updated `README.md` with DTC section and usage examples
- Added build rules documentation (5 core requirements for source and binary management)
- Added `dtc-1.7.2.tar.gz` to archive source list
- Updated `archive/SHA256SUMS` with DTC source checksum

### Fixed
- Static linking now correctly produces pure static binaries without .so files
- Dynamic binary testing uses musl interpreter for compatibility on glibc systems
- MUSL_SYSROOT environment variable properly set for test execution

## [v15.1.0-musl-gcc] - 2025-xx-xx

### Added
- musl cross-compilation toolchain v15.1.0
  - GCC 15.1.0
  - Binutils 2.44
  - musl 1.2.6
  - Linux headers 5.8.5
  - Support for x86_64, ARM, AArch64, RISC-V 64 architectures
  - Three variants: debug, nodebug, lto-nodebug

## [v5.3-bash] - 2024-xx-xx

### Added
- Bash 5.3 cross-compilation support
  - Official patches bash53-001 through bash53-015
  - Dynamic and static linking variants
  - Multibyte and built-in readline/history support
  - No NLS, OpenSSL, or ncurses dependencies

## [v2.12-wpa_supplicant] - 2024-xx-xx

### Added
- wpa_supplicant 2.12 toolchain package
  - hostapd and hostapd_cli
  - wpa_supplicant and wpa_cli
  - dhcpcd with privilege separation support
  - libnl 3.12.0 for dynamic builds
  - Internal TLS/crypto implementation (no OpenSSL)
  - WPA/WPA2, WPS, PMF, nl80211 support

## [v2026.92-dropbear] - 2024-xx-xx

### Added
- Dropbear 2026.92 SSH server/client
  - dropbear (SSH server daemon)
  - dbclient (SSH client)
  - dropbearkey, dropbearconvert, scp
  - BusyBox-compatible init.d scripts
  - Auto-generation of Ed25519, ECDSA, RSA host keys
  - sshd_config template for compatibility

## [v15.1-gdb] - 2024-xx-xx

### Added
- GDB 15.1 debugger with gdbserver
  - Full-featured gdb for host debugging
  - gdbserver for remote target debugging
  - Static and dynamic linking variants

## [v1.38.0-busybox] - 2024-xx-xx

### Added
- BusyBox 1.38.0 with complete ash shell
  - Static single-binary builds
  - Dynamic builds with complete rootfs
  - Unicode, locale, wide-character support
  - Chinese UTF-8 line editing in ash
  - SysV-style init.d system
  - DHCP, telnet, TFTP server support
  - mdev device manager
  - Comprehensive `/etc` templates with secure defaults

### Changed
- Disabled hush shell (ash only)
- Locked privilege-separation accounts (sshd, dhcpcd) with UID/GID
- Network configuration via BusyBox ifupdown with `/etc/network/interface`
- BusyBox init.d script conventions documented in `docs/busybox-init.d.md`

---

## Release Tag Conventions

Each software component uses independent workflow and tag format:

```
v<version>-<software>
```

Examples:
- `v1.7.2-dtc` - DTC (Device Tree Compiler)
- `v5.3-bash` - Bash shell
- `v1.38.0-busybox` - BusyBox utilities
- `v2026.92-dropbear` - Dropbear SSH
- `v15.1-gdb` - GDB debugger
- `v2.12-wpa_supplicant` - wpa_supplicant + hostapd + dhcpcd
- `v15.1.0-musl-gcc` - musl cross-compilation toolchain

## Architecture Support

All software builds target:
- `x86_64-linux-musl`
- `arm-linux-musleabi`
- `aarch64-linux-musl`
- `riscv64-linux-musl`

## Link Type Variants

- **static**: Fully static linking with no runtime dependencies
- **dynamic**: Dynamically linked to musl libc (requires musl loader and libc.so)
